Z||000005||Oreif||02-02-2001||11:18 AM||||Sounds like a vacuum leak. Possible the EGR itself isn't sealing or one of the thermal vacuum switches.||||reg||1
Z||000006||theogre||02-02-2001||08:13 PM||||Cam and lifters are replaced as a set. If you put new lifters on an old cam, the cam likely won't last long.<P>I wouldn't be driving it far with the problems you are having. The screaching could be the belt. could also be a bearing in the water pump or alt.||||reg||1
Z||000007||HAGS||02-03-2001||03:46 AM||||The belt was off and the alternator was very loose when I got to autozone, picked up everything so I could work on it...replaced the air intake hose and didnt get the vacuum sound...was going to replace vacuum hoses but they didnt have any that size...they broke when I was fixing the alternator and had to jerry-rig some rubber hoses in their place...anyway on the way home sounded like something gave out and the engine died...put it in nuetral and looked in the rear view mirror and biggest cloud of smoke I'd seen come from a car, coasted to the gas station but the brakes were working at about 10% power after this happend and almost hit several things.  Tried to restart and only get half a crank.||||reg||1
